# Hook authoring rules

`hooks.json` only wires `block-dangerous` (beforeShellExecution) and
`block-env-read` (beforeReadFile). Those two are the product's hook-interop
reference, not a conductor. Do not re-add engineering-loop hooks
(`goal-audit-gate`, `log-trajectory`, `protect-loop-core`, `verify-gate`,
`record-session`, `format-and-typecheck`). See
[0014](../../docs/decisions/0014-pstack-only-no-engineering-loop.md).

## Hook input arrives as JSON on stdin

Cursor delivers the payload on stdin, not as environment variables. Scripts must
`ConvertFrom-Json` / parse stdin. A hook that only reads `$env:SOMETHING` is a
no-op.

## `.cursor/hooks/*.ps1` must be ASCII-only

Windows PowerShell 5.1 decodes a `.ps1` with no BOM as cp1252, so a non-ASCII
character inside a string literal breaks the script.

## Do not chain `bash || pwsh`

A failing bash script with a missing `pwsh` would hide the real exit code.
`hooks.json` calls each `.ps1` via `powershell -File`. `grep -c '||' .cursor/hooks.json`
returns 0 and must stay 0.
